{
	title: 'Restart scopes: local, host, both, all',
	spec: 'The shared command list has one /restart command with scopes. Bare /restart means /restart all, in the terminal and on the web. /restart local (Ctrl-R) restarts only this client: the terminal exits with the restart code (the host too, if this client is it), the web page reloads. Ctrl-R is /restart local everywhere: the terminal emergency path, and an explicit page reload on the web, including macOS where native Ctrl-R does not reload. The web handles Ctrl-R before modal, question and editor keys, saves any current composer draft, and reloads only this page without a host command; Cmd-R and Ctrl-Alt-R remain native. Terminal raw-input scanning and browser events use one browser-safe emergency-key rule and synchronous dispatcher in src/common/emergency.ts, with platform callbacks for restart. Ctrl-R, including Shift/Caps Lock variants, always restarts the local client before stateful UI handling; /keys shows it as /restart local (command-list keyArgs), and completion offers local, host, both and all. /restart host, both and all run on the host (src/host/commands/restart.ts), which replies and then exits with the restart code after a short flush delay; peers take over as usual, whichever wins, whatever code it runs. both: the client that typed it marks itself and restarts (terminal) as soon as its link changes after the mark, or reloads (web) once the host is gone and back. all: the host first sends every connected client a restart event, which marks it the same way. Delivery to connected clients is best effort: a client asleep or disconnected then is not tracked. When the client is the host process, local and host restart the same process once. Existing command ids, takeover and turn recovery are reused; restart adds no new lifecycle state or permission tier.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'Host code may not import client code (conventions.test.ts layers): the host command exits through restartProcess.run, which main.ts points at terminal.restart so raw mode is left first. Web restart state lives in src/web/restart.ts, and the web draft store in src/web/draft-store.ts, keeping web/app.ts under the 400-line limit.',
		'Restored invariant: Ctrl-R uses the same synchronous emergency dispatcher in both clients, ahead of UI state. Moved the existing raw scanner to common/emergency.ts; native TextDecoder replaces Buffer so the browser can import it. Browser Ctrl-C/Z stay native, while Ctrl-R (Shift and Caps Lock included) invokes the local reload callback. The previous browser-native-reload exception failed on macOS.'
